    "body": "## Motivation\n\nNPU decode and target-verify graph replay require host-side sequence lengths\nto update graph inputs. Reading these lengths through\n`forward_batch.seq_lens.cpu()` introduces a blocking device-to-host copy,\neven when the batch already provides a CPU mirror.\n\nReuse the existing CPU mirror to avoid this redundant synchronization and\nreduce host-side stalls during graph replay preparation.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Prefer `forward_batch.seq_lens_cpu` when preparing sequence lengths for\n  NPU decode and target-verify graph replay.\n- Slice the CPU mirror to the active batch size before adding graph padding.\n- Preserve the captured verify-width adjustment for target verification.\n- Preserve the existing DFlash metadata path.\n- Retain the device-to-host fallback when `seq_lens_cpu` is unavailable.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAccuracy evaluation of the final graph-runner-only patch is pending.\n\nPrevious accuracy runs included an additional FutureMap change that has\nsince been reverted, so those results do not validate the final patch.\n\nCompleted static checks:\n\n- Python syntax validation.\n- `git diff --check`.\n- AST comparison confirming that the subsequent comment cleanup did not\n  change executable code.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nBenchmarking and profiling of the final graph-runner-only patch are pending.\n\nThe previous combined-patch performance results are excluded because they\ndo not isolate the benefit of the retained change.\n\nPlanned validation:\n\n- Compare the parent commit against this patch under identical model,\n  workload, and server settings.\n- Measure TPOT and output token throughput.\n- Inspect NPU traces for host-side D2H synchronization and device idle gaps\n  around graph replay preparation.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Run repository formatting and pre-commit checks.\n- [ ] Add or run relevant regression tests.\n- [ ] Confirm whether documentation updates are required.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy results for the final patch.\n- [ ] Provide speed benchmark and profiling results for the final patch.\n- [ ] Verify compliance with the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39252923886](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39252923886)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39252924088](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39252924088)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39252923947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39252923947)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
